               event time (RMET) is an easily interpretable, clinically
               meaningful summary of the survival function in the presence of
               censoring. The RMET is the average of all potential event times
               measured up to a time point τ and can be estimated consistently
               by the area under the Kaplan-Meier curve over $[0, \tau ]$. In
